{"id":"rtpr.8","n":"rtpr","s":"8","src":{"u":{"pkg":"iproute2","ver":"5.15.0-1ubuntu2.2","repo":"jammy-updates/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/i/iproute2/iproute2_5.15.0-1ubuntu2.2_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/rtpr.8.gz","sha256":"9e9d6354e9d32683e56191ef6638e37e73698daa9b7765e2563b38eff34b0890","date":"18 September, 2015","origin":""}},"nopt":{"u":0},"miss":{"u":["--oneline"]},"desc":"replace backslashes with newlines.","u":[["NAME","<p>rtpr - replace backslashes with newlines.</p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p><b>rtpr</b> is a trivial shell script which converts backslashes in standard input to newlines. It's sole purpose is to be fed with input from <b>ip</b> when executed with it's <b>--oneline</b> flag.</p>"],["EXAMPLES","<dl><dt>ip --oneline address show | rtpr</dt><dd>Undo oneline converted <b>ip-address</b> output.</dd></dl>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>ip</b>(8)</p>"],["AUTHORS","<p>Stephen Hemminger &lt;shemming@brocade.com&gt;</p>"]]}